<title>UK: EU may rule Boeing/Mcdonnell merger illegal - report.</title>
<headline>EU may rule Boeing/Mcdonnell merger illegal - report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union may declare a planned merger between U.S. aerospace giants Boeing and McDonnell Douglas illegal, the Financial Times reported on Monday.</p>
<p>The newspaper said European Commission officials were warning privately that the merger may be opposed if the two companies ignored EU concerns about the deal's impact on competition.</p>
<p>The Financial Times said the new aerospace group could in theory face a fine in the region of $5.0 billion if the Commission took a tough line. The EU would detail its objections to the merger this week, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Last week, European competition director Jonathan Faull said the EU had the right to review and, if necessary, block the merger between Boeing and McDonnell Douglas.</p>
</text>
